<section class="card">
<h2>Welcome to Our Security Tools Centre</h2>

<p>
Kibeere Cybersecurity Academy provides educational information
about cybersecurity applications, software and digital protection
technologies. Our objective is to help beginners, students,
professionals and businesses understand the tools available
for improving their digital security.
</p>

<p>
Modern technology makes communication, education, business
and online services easier. However, these activities also
introduce security challenges such as malware, phishing,
unauthorised access, data theft and network attacks.
</p>

<p>
Our security tools centre explores different categories of
software, explains their purposes and provides links to
official resources where readers can learn more.
</p>

<h3>What You Will Discover</h3>
<ul>
<li>Antivirus and endpoint protection software.</li>
<li>Firewalls and network security technologies.</li>
<li>Network monitoring and packet analysis tools.</li>
<li>Vulnerability assessment software.</li>
<li>Password and account protection solutions.</li>
<li>VPN and internet privacy services.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>1. Antivirus Software</h2>
<p>
Antivirus software helps detect, prevent and remove malicious
programmes such as viruses, spyware, trojans and ransomware.
It is an important part of protecting supported computers.
</p>

<h3>Examples</h3>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/comprehensive-security" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Defender</a> – built-in Windows security protection.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.bitdefender.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bitdefender</a> – antivirus and security products.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.avast.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Avast</a> – consumer security software.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>2. Firewalls</h2>
<p>
Firewalls control incoming and outgoing network traffic
according to configured security rules. They help prevent
unwanted network connections.
</p>

<h3>Examples</h3>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.pfsense.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pfSense</a> – firewall and routing platform.</li>
<li><a href="https://opnsense.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OPNsense</a> – open-source firewall software.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Security</a> – Windows security resources.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>3. Network Monitoring and Analysis</h2>
<p>
Network monitoring tools help administrators understand
network traffic, investigate connection problems and identify
unusual activity.
</p>

<h3>Examples</h3>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.wireshark.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wireshark</a> – network packet analysis.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.zabbix.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zabbix</a> – infrastructure and network monitoring.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.ntop.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ntop</a> – network traffic monitoring.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>4. Vulnerability Assessment Tools</h2>
<p>
Vulnerability assessment tools help identify potential
weaknesses in computer systems, applications and networks.
Their results can help administrators improve security.
</p>

<h3>Examples</h3>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://nmap.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nmap</a> – network discovery and security auditing.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.tenable.com/products/nessus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nessus</a> – vulnerability scanning.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.openvas.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenVAS</a> – vulnerability assessment technology.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>5. Password and Account Security</h2>
<p>
Password managers help users create and manage strong,
unique passwords. Multi-factor authentication adds another
layer of protection to online accounts.
</p>
<p>
Read our <a href="password-managers.html">Password Manager Guide</a>
to understand popular password management services.
</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>6. VPN and Privacy Tools</h2>
<p>
VPN services can encrypt supported internet traffic between
a user's device and a VPN server. They may provide additional
privacy features when browsing online.
</p>
<p>
Explore our <a href="vpn-reviews.html">VPN Reviews and Comparisons</a>
to learn about selected VPN providers.
</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>How to Choose Security Software</h2>
<ul>
<li>Identify the security problem you want to solve.</li>
<li>Check software compatibility with your device.</li>
<li>Compare free and paid features.</li>
<li>Read the provider's privacy policy.</li>
<li>Research independent security assessments.</li>
<li>Check update frequency and customer support.</li>
<li>Download applications from official sources.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h2>Responsible Use of Security Tools</h2>
<div class="notice">
Only scan, monitor or test computers and networks that
you own or have explicit permission to assess. Use
cybersecurity software responsibly and respect other
people's privacy.
</div>
</section>

